<div class="content-box" style="background: #fff3cd; border-left: 4px solid #ffc107;">
    <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> Watch Out For</h2>
    <p>Common misconceptions to avoid:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Decomposition ≠ Breaking down code:</strong> Decomposition happens <em>before</em> you write any code. You break down the <em>problem</em>, not the program!</li>
        <li><strong>Abstraction ≠ Making things complicated:</strong> Abstraction means <em>removing</em> irrelevant details to focus on what matters.</li>
        <li><strong>Flowchart branches:</strong> Always label your decision branches with True/False or Yes/No. Never leave flowlines disconnected!</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class="content-box">
    <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-brain"></i> Big Ideas to Think About</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>"The map is not the territory"</strong> - When we abstract, we simplify reality. Does this help or limit our understanding?</li>
        <li>When we name and categorise a problem in a specification, does that "lock" us into certain solutions?</li>
    </ul>
</div>

